course: dictionary
lesson: 2516
title: Deciduous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deciduous is a science word. The clue is in the sentence: «Deciduous trees, like oak, maple and birch, drop their leaves in autumn and rest through winter.» The words drop their leaves in autumn tell you what deciduous means.
explain: Look for a word that is set against it. «Evergreen trees, like pine and spruce, keep their needles all year.» Evergreen means the opposite: it keeps its leaves. When two words are compared, the contrast is a strong clue to meaning.
explain: The word can also describe teeth. «Deciduous teeth» are baby teeth that fall out to make room for adult teeth. Ask yourself what would fit: a tree that loses its leaves and a tooth that falls out and is replaced both show the same idea of falling out.
fact: Deciduous means losing all your leaves every autumn and growing new ones in spring.
fact: «Deciduous» trees include oak, maple and birch.
fact: Evergreen trees, like pine and spruce, keep their needles all year.
fact: Deciduous teeth are baby teeth, and they fall out to make room for adult teeth.
fact: Deciduous trees drop their leaves in autumn, which helps them save water in winter.
exercise: «Deciduous trees lose all their leaves in autumn.» What does deciduous mean? | Living under water | *Losing all their leaves every autumn | Growing very tall and thin | Keeping their needles all year
exercise: «Evergreen trees, like pine and spruce, keep their needles all year.» Which of these is a deciduous tree? | Fir | *Birch | Pine | Spruce
exercise: Mia says deciduous teeth are wobbly grown-up teeth. What are deciduous teeth really? | Very sharp adult teeth | *Baby teeth that fall out to make room for adult teeth | Teeth made of wood | Teeth that never fall out
test: Why do deciduous trees drop their leaves in autumn? | To make their bark shine | *To help save water when the ground is frozen | To grow taller in winter | To hide from birds
test: Which of these trees is NOT deciduous? | Birch | *Pine | Maple | Oak
exam: Which sentence uses deciduous correctly? | Deciduous means a grey, wet day in Scotland | Deciduous trees grow only in deserts | The spruce is deciduous because it keeps its needles all year | *In autumn the maple lost all its leaves, so it is deciduous
